# Architecture and Code Organization Rules

## Code Organization

- Keep commands in separate files under src/commands/
- Keep providers in separate files under src/providers/
- Use barrel exports (index.ts) for clean imports
- Separate utilities into src/utils/ directory
- Follow single responsibility principle

## File Structure

- Use consistent naming conventions
- Group related functionality together
- Keep files focused and manageable
- Use TypeScript modules properly
- Maintain clear separation of concerns

## Extension Architecture

- Implement proper activation and deactivation
- Use VSCode API patterns consistently
- Register commands and providers properly
- Handle extension lifecycle correctly
- Use proper disposal patterns

## Code Quality

- Write self-documenting code with clear variable names
- Keep functions small and focused
- Use meaningful function and variable names
- Add JSDoc comments for public APIs
- Follow consistent code style

## Modularity

- Create reusable utility functions
- Use dependency injection where appropriate
- Avoid tight coupling between modules
- Use composition over inheritance
- Keep interfaces clean and minimal

